# Row witnesses for fusion of two local kernel elements

Put u=(xy)^14 and v=u*(x⁻¹*u*x). The tables witness
(u*(ababb)^5)^15=1 and (v*a)^11=1. These odd exponents provide
conjugators inside the generated matrix group once the products are checked.
The input rows and local words are from the ATLAS certificates documented in
`Cardinality.Subgroup`. The generator in `source/generate.py` is untrusted;
`Products` checks every multiplication using Lean's kernel.
